-- title:
--   Points of formally smooth algebras lift along p-adic reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a natural number, and let $k$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra such that the structure map $\mathcal O \to k$ is surjective with kernel exactly the ideal generated by $p$, so that $k$ is identified with $\mathcal O/p\mathcal O$; assume moreover that $\mathcal O$ is adically complete (complete and separated) for the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is formally smooth over $\mathcal O$, and let $Y$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module. Then for every $k$-algebra homomorphism $\chi \colon k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R \to k \otimes_{\mathcal O} Y$ between the reductions there exists an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $x \colon \mathcal R \to Y$ whose base change along $\mathcal O \to k$, namely the map $k \otimes_{\mathcal O} \mathcal R \to k \otimes_{\mathcal O} Y$ induced by the identity of $k$ and by $x$, equals $\chi$. Only existence of such a lift $x$ is asserted, not uniqueness; $p$ is not assumed prime.
--
--   This is the formal-smoothness lifting criterion for points with values in a finite free algebra over a $p$-adically complete base (EGA IV, 0.19.3.10), equivalently the smooth — in particular the finite étale — case of Fontaine's description of the $Y$-valued points of a finite flat group scheme in terms of points of its special fibre. It is used to obtain the corresponding existence-and-uniqueness statement for formally étale algebras over $\mathbf Z/p$-type reductions, [`Algebra.FormallyEtale.existsUnique_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_module_finite_free_zmodp`](thm.html#Algebra.FormallyEtale.existsUnique_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_module_finite_free_zmodp).
